.TH OMNICALC 1 "2026-11-25" "omnicalc 2026.11.18" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omnicalc \- high-performance scientific CLI calculator, unit converter, and CAS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omnicalc
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIEXPRESSION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omnicalc
is an offline-first scientific command-line calculator, dimensional unit converter,
linear algebra engine, and symbolic Computer Algebra System (CAS) written in Rust.
When invoked without an expression on a terminal, it starts an interactive REPL.
When standard input is piped, it evaluates each non-empty, non-comment line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-eval " " \fIEXPR\fR
Evaluate the specified mathematical expression directly.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-raw
Print raw numeric values without unit labels or formatting decoration.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-base " " \fIBASE\fR
Output integers in \fBdec\fR (default), \fBhex\fR, \fBbin\fR, or \fBoct\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-completions " " \fISHELL\fR
Generate shell completion scripts to stdout for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, \fBfish\fR,
\fBpowershell\fR, or \fBelvish\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-update\-rates
Opt-in network command to fetch daily European Central Bank (ECB) exchange rates
and cache them locally to \fI~/.cache/omnicalc/rates.json\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-credits ", " \-\-about
Display authorship, acknowledgments, and architectural origins.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print CLI usage summary.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print package version.
.SH OPERATOR PRECEDENCE
From lowest to highest binding precedence:
.TP
.B 1. Equation & Conversion:
\fB=\fR, \fBto\fR, \fBas\fR, \fBin\fR, \fB\->\fR
.TP
.B 2. Bitwise OR / XOR / AND / Shifts:
\fB|\fR < \fB^^\fR (\fBxor\fR) < \fB&\fR < \fB<<\fR, \fB>>\fR
.TP
.B 3. Uncertainty:
\fB±\fR, \fB+/-\fR (Gaussian absolute error propagation)
.TP
.B 4. Addition & Subtraction:
\fB+\fR, \fB-\fR
.TP
.B 5. Multiplication, Division, Modulo, Percentage:
\fB*\fR, \fB/\fR, \fB%\fR, \fBof\fR
.TP
.B 6. Implicit Multiplication:
\fB2x\fR, \fB100 J / 10 s\fR (binds tighter than explicit \fB/\fR and \fB*\fR)
.TP
.B 7. Exponentiation & Postfix:
\fB^\fR, \fB**\fR (right-associative), \fB%\fR (postfix), \fB'\fR (derivative)
.SH UNITS & CONSTANTS
Supports 200+ SI base and derived units across length, mass, time, current,
affine temperature (\fBdegC\fR, \fBdegF\fR, \fBK\fR), energy, power, pressure,
digital storage, data rates, and currencies (\fBUSD\fR, \fBEUR\fR, \fBGBP\fR,
\fBJPY\fR, \fBINR\fR, \fBCAD\fR, \fBAUD\fR, \fBCHF\fR, \fBCNY\fR).
Built-in constants: \fBpi\fR (\fBπ\fR), \fBtau\fR (\fBτ\fR), \fBphi\fR (\fBφ\fR),
\fBe\fR, \fBc\fR (speed of light), and \fBi\fR (imaginary unit).
.SH CALCULUS & LINEAR ALGEBRA
.TP
.B diff(expr[, var])
Symbolic differentiation.
.TP
.B int(expr, lower, upper) / integrate(expr; lower; upper)
Definite numerical integration via Composite Simpson's Rule.
.TP
.B factor(expr[, var])
Integer prime factorization and quadratic polynomial factoring.
.TP
.B solve(eq[, var]) / solve([eq1, eq2, ...], [v1, v2, ...])
Single-variable linear/quadratic/Newton-Raphson solver and multi-variable linear system solver.
.TP
.B Vectors & Matrices:
Bracket syntax \fB[1, 2, 3]\fR and \fB[[1, 2], [3, 4]]\fR with \fBdot\fR, \fBcross\fR,
\fBnorm\fR, \fBdet\fR, \fBinv\fR, and \fBtranspose\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.omnicalc_history
Interactive REPL command history.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/omnicalc/rates.json
Optional local ECB currency cache populated only by \fB\-\-update\-rates\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful evaluation or command completion.
.TP
.B 1
Syntax, domain, dimensional, I/O, or evaluation error.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line flags or arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
omnicalc -e "100 km/h to m/s"
omnicalc -e "20 degC - 10 degC"
omnicalc -e "int(sin(x), 0, pi)"
omnicalc -e "solve([2x + y = 7, x - y = 2], [x, y])"
omnicalc --completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/omnicalc
.fi
